{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"6f6c1958-24d5-4340-888a-dc6199186fc9","step":{"id":"s1","script":"Slope-intercept form describes a straight line. The number b tells us where the line crosses the vertical axis.","ops":[{"op":"equation","id":"form","region":"A1","latex":"y=mx+b"},{"op":"figure","id":"graph","region":"right","frame":{"x":[-1,4],"y":[-1,9],"axes":"edge","x_label":"x","y_label":"y"},"marks":[{"kind":"fn","id":"line","y":"2*x+1","domain":[-1,4]},{"kind":"point","id":"intercept","at":{"on":"line","x":0},"label":"(0, 1)"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"bvalue","anchor":{"el":"form","side":"below","gap":0.12},"latex":"b=1\\quad\\text{(vertical intercept)}"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"6f6c1958-24d5-4340-888a-dc6199186fc9","step":{"id":"s2","script":"The slope m measures rise divided by run. From this intercept, moving one unit right takes us two units up.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"triangle","on":"graph","marks":[{"kind":"point","id":"next","at":{"on":"line","x":1},"label":"(1, 3)"},{"kind":"segment","id":"run","from":{"at":"intercept"},"to":[1,1],"stroke":"dashed","label":"run = 1"},{"kind":"segment","id":"rise","from":[1,1],"to":{"at":"next"},"stroke":"dashed","label":"rise = 2"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"slope","anchor":{"el":"bvalue","side":"below","gap":0.12},"latex":"m=\\frac{\\text{rise}}{\\text{run}}=\\frac{2}{1}=2"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"6f6c1958-24d5-4340-888a-dc6199186fc9","step":{"id":"s3","script":"Substitute the slope and intercept to get y equals two x plus one. At x equals three, what y value should we plot?","ops":[{"op":"equation","id":"example","anchor":{"el":"slope","side":"below","gap":0.12},"latex":"y=2x+1"},{"op":"figure","id":"guide","on":"graph","marks":[{"kind":"segment","from":[3,0],"to":{"on":"line","x":3},"stroke":"dashed"},{"kind":"text","at":[3.35,4],"text":"x = 3","size":"small"}]}],"checkpoint":{"question":"For y = 2x + 1, what is y when x = 3?","expected_gist":"y = 2(3) + 1 = 7."}}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"6f6c1958-24d5-4340-888a-dc6199186fc9","step":{"id":"s4","script":"Three runs of one give a total rise of six. Starting at one, we reach seven, so the point is three, seven.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"answer","on":"graph","marks":[{"kind":"point","at":{"on":"line","x":3},"label":"(3, 7)"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"evaluate","anchor":{"el":"example","side":"below","gap":0.12},"latex":"x=3\\;\\Rightarrow\\;y=2(3)+1=7"}],"checkpoint":null}}
